WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
He was vice president.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.268
Kamala Harris is

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.004
scheduled to be meeting this morning

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.672
with Thailand's prime minister.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.639
She's been in Bangkok

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.607
representing the U.S.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.808
at the Asia-Pacific

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.276
Economic Cooperation Summit,

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.945
which just concluded

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:12.879
Chinese President

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.447
Xi Jinping is also there.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.250
And on Saturday, the two spoke briefly.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.486
Well, afterwards, the vice president

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.187
tweeted that during their exchange,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.989
she reiterated the importance

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.624
of open communications

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.026
to manage competition

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.228
between the two countries.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.362
Harris also condemned

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.398
North Korea's latest missile launch.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.365
On Friday,

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.167
the young daughter of

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.402
North Korea's leader

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.470
made her first public appearance

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.938
during that launch.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:39.806
These images appeared

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.940
to show them holding hands

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.674
as they inspect

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.675
a powerful

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.778
intercontinental ballistic missile.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.248
CNN's Will Ripley has more

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:48.882
U.S.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.016
Vice President Kamala Harris

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:50.750
and Chinese President

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.284
Xi Jinping

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.419
exchanged brief words

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:53.553
on the sidelines of the APEC

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.921
summit here in Bangkok,

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:55.989
talking about the importance

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.357
of avoiding conflict

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.192
and encouraging cooperation

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.794
on issues of global concern.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:01.961
That's according to Chinese state media

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.130
as readout of the brief conversation.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.031
One issue, though,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.965
that the United States

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.268
and China are not really cooperating

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.103
on is the issue of North Korea,

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.371
which has been launching missiles

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.672
at an unprecedented pace

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.807
throughout the year,

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.542
including this ICBM

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.076
launch of what

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:16.810
North Korea calls

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.978
a new kind of long range missile

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:19.913
capable of striking,

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.281
according to the Japanese government,

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.382
pretty much anywhere

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.950
in the United States

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.418
and potentially most of the world,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.654
excluding some portions of South America.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.556
If you look at the possible

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.291
trajectory, distance of this missile

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.559
that was tested

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.662
and the missile test was pretty striking,

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.596
when you look at the photos

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.630
released by North Korean state

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.132
media on Saturday morning,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.600
it was rising up of the over

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.001
the shoot on area of Pyongyang near

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.903
the Pyongyang International Airport.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.271
Kim Jong un, the North Korean leader,

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.239
was there with his wife.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.507
And for the first time,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.142
his daughter, believed to be around

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.176
nine years old,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.312
identified by North Korean state media

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.280
and appearing right alongside her dad

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.415
as they walked around.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.916
This gigantic missile

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.852
dwarfed by the size of the

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.020
transporter erector launch vehicle

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.922
that was used to fire the missile.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.493
Basically more than 3700 miles

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.695
or 6000 kilometers up into space

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.430
before a splashdown in the waters

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.598
near Japan.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.932
Had the trajectory been different,

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.067
the missile could have traveled

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:14.734
much farther,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.102
the Japanese government warns.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:16.903
And yet

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.037
there has really been little

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.006
in terms of substantive consequences

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:20.807
this year

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.108
with all of these North Korean

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.277
missile launch events. At least 34.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.478
If you look at the calendar

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.613
and some of those days, North Korea

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.381
launching multiple missiles at once.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.616
North Korea claiming to have launched

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.984
around 50 ballistic missiles

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.018
so far this year.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.020
That's more than any other year

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.421
in North Korean history.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.223
And certainly it comes at a time

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.258
that there are growing concerns

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.160
about a seventh underground nuclear test.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.662
And the fact of the matter is China,

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.897
which does have the ability

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.198
to heavily enforce sanctions

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.666
and put pressure on North Korea

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.934
from the perspective of the U.S.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.869
and its allies, is simply not doing that.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:50.837
China and Russia

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.505
with veto power at the United Nations

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.640
Security Council,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.774
are basically saying

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.843
that all sides need to remain calm,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.610
even though the U.S.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.778
says it's North Korea

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.880
that continues to provoke the situation.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.515
Will Ripley, CNN, Bangkok.

